{
  "0": "Across all four categories, replace tied unit normalization with e/sqrt(max(||e||2,1e-8)), preserving zero padding (embedding direction). Jointly set Adam LR=0.0005, dropout=0.05 and batch size=256 (hyperparameter direction). Partial normalization retains item-specific magnitude while moderating raw scale; lower dropout preserves weaker recurrent inputs, and larger batches with smaller steps may stabilize their optimization. Retain the incumbent mixed loss, GRU topology, width and history window.",
  "1": "Across all four categories, untie history and target/candidate embedding tables, unit-normalizing both and initializing them identically (embedding). Replace the pairwise term with softplus(0.5+negative-positive), retaining the 0.2 pointwise term (objective). Set LR=0.0007 and dropout=0.15 (hyperparameters). Separate input/output roles may reduce conflicting gradients; the ranking margin encourages separation, while slower updates and stronger dropout constrain the added parameters. Preserve GRU topology, history and sampling.",
  "2": "Across all four categories, add an 8-dimensional learned embedding of floor(log2(1+training_item_count)), projected into history inputs only (features). Normalize tied item embeddings to fixed norm 0.75, keeping padding zero (embedding). Use softplus((negative-positive)/0.75) plus the incumbent 0.2 pointwise term (objective). Set LR=0.0006 and dropout=0.05 (hyperparameters). Learned frequency context may distinguish common from rare observations; lower temperature counteracts reduced embedding scale, while smaller steps stabilize joint fitting. Preserve GRU topology and sampling; save frequency bins and update the predictor writer.",
  "3": "Across all four categories, replace tied unit-normalized embeddings with ordinary trainable tied embeddings initialized as in the incumbent, preserving zero padding (embedding). Use softplus(negative-positive)+0.2*[softplus(-positive)+softplus(negative)] plus 1e-4 times the mean squared norm of nonpadding history, positive and negative embeddings (objective). Free item magnitudes may capture confidence lost through unit normalization; explicit norm regularization may control score inflation. Keep all optimizer settings, GRU topology, sampling and history unchanged."
}
